ets give Democrats only about a one-in-ten chance.\n\nStill, the contest has drawn unusual attention. Democratic-sponsored polls show Hyde-Smith in the low-to-mid 40s with leads of three to six points, Colom has raised $2.4 million, and outside groups are spending to support him and attack the incumbent. Cory Booker has campaigned with Colom in the race's final month. No independent polling confirms a close race, and Hyde-Smith's cash advantage and Mississippi's partisan baseline keep her ahead, but the final margin may run tighter than her past double-digit wins.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0354, "margin": -10.93}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0478, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0452, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0712, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0338, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0525, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0557, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0878, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0513, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.051, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0903, "margin": -9.5}]}